        {
          "id": "el-1790869896708-bbbzp7cqh",
          "type": "text",
          "content": "<div>In order for <b>everybody</b> to always get the <b>same</b> <b>result</b>, we have <b>agreed</b> on a set of <b>rules</b> that apply to the <b>Order of Operations</b>.</div><div><br></div><div>These rules are sometimes called <b>PEMDAS</b> (<b>P</b>arenthesis, <b>E</b>xponents, <b>M</b>ultiplication, <b>D</b>ivision, <b>A</b>ddition, <b>S</b>ubtraction)</div>",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 64.0625,
